            <ArticleTitle>[Wernicke´s encephalopathy and polyneuropathy associated with vitamin B complex deficiency after a bariatric surgery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>474-84</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1590/S0120-41572012000400002</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0120-41572012000400002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bariatric surgery is a treatment that guarantees a substantial and lasting weight loss in addition to the tangible benefits relating to obesity-associated medical conditions. The increasing number of bariatric surgeries has revealed an increasing number of complications related to this procedure, including Wernicke´s encephalopathy and vitamin B deficiency polyneuropathies. Herein, a 7-week post-surgery case of Wernicke´s encephalopathy is presented that emphasizes the importance of an early recognition of these symptoms so as to initiate intervention during the reversible phase of these potentially lethal pathologies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
